~~Note that the _ngc_ output contains `directives: [i1.NgForOf]`, which is missing from the code inside of `vendor-es2015.js` when using the CLI. This piece of generated code would have enabled the component to use the `NgForOf` directive at runtime, so it being elided will prevent it from being used at runtime.~~

~~I have no clue why all of the directives get elided. The Angular compiler does generate the `directives: [i1.NgForOf]` code regardless of ngc vs CLI, and the emitted source file emitted from ngtsc does also contain that piece of code. So, it appears as if some transform later in the pipeline elides it from the code.~~

